INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('309','1','en','Full Day Chobe Trip — Botswana','chobe-day-trip-1','<p>Cross into Botswana for a full day at world-famous Chobe National Park — home to the greatest elephant concentration on earth. Morning 4x4 game drive followed by an afternoon Chobe River boat cruise watching elephant herds swim across.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('310','2','en','Helicopter Flight over Victoria Falls','helicopter-flight-victoria-falls','<p>Experience the grandeur of Victoria Falls from above on a breathtaking helicopter flight — one of the most spectacular aviation experiences in the world. Hover above one of the Seven Natural Wonders as the mighty Zambezi River plunges 108 metres into the gorge below. Choose your flight duration: 12/13 minutes for the classic scenic loop, or extend to 25 minutes for a full Zambezi gorge experience.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('311','3','en','Tour Victoria Falls','tour-victoria-falls-3','Discover how Victoria Falls was formed and what local customs and traditions surround them. It is well worth booking a Pearls Tourss Zambian Tour of the Falls.

Described by the Kololo tribe living in the area in the 1800’s as ‘Mosi-oa-Tunya’ – ‘the Smoke that Thunders’ and in more modern terms as ‘the greatest known curtain of falling water’. Victoria Falls are a spectacular sight of awe-inspiring beauty and grandeur on the Zambezi River, bordering Zambia and Zimbabwe.

A path along the edge of the forest provides the visitor, who is prepared to brave the tremendous spray with an unparalleled series of views of the Falls. One special vantage point is across the Knife edge bridge, where visitors can have the finest view of the Eastern Cataract and the Main Falls as well as the Boiling Pot where the river turns and heads down the Batoka Gorge.
Other vantage points include the Falls bridge and the Lookout Tree which commands a panoramic view across the Main Falls. Different times of the year will provide completely different experiences of the Falls region.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('312','4','en','White Water Rafting — Zambezi River','white-water-rafting-5','<p>The Zambezi below Victoria Falls offers world-class Grade 5 white water rafting through the dramatic Batoka Gorge. Paddle through rapids rated among the best in the world, with your experienced guide leading you through a full day of river adventure.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('313','5','en','Flying Fox','flying-fox-6','Imagine taking a running jump into thin air over the chasm, soaring horizontally through the air over the turmoil of the Zambezi below. The gorge at this point is 200 meters wide and 120 meters deep. This is a great appetizer before you try the Zip Line and Gorge Swing.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('314','6','en','Canopy Tour','canopy-tour-7','Observe the riverine forest from a variety of different vantage points – from above, below and within the canopy itself. Experience forest bird-life, which can include the Knysna and Purple crested Turaco (Lourie) and Peregrine Falcons. The Victoria Falls Canopy Tour offers a network of slides, trails and rope bridge walkways within the canopy of the hardwood forest of the Zambezi gorges.This experience is suitable to adventure seekers of all ages including families and groups. This is family fun with a unique birds-eye view of one the seven natural wonders of the world.

The Canopy Tour consists of nine slides, varying in length and 1 cable bridge walkway. The longest slide is about 85 metres long and the shortest 40 metres in length. Our friendly and experienced staff will give you a detailed safety briefing before the canopy tour, taking you step by step through your upcoming adventure. There are two guides on each tour and the activity lasts for between two to two and a half hours.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('315','7','en','ZipLine','zipline-8','This is the longest Zip Line (Foofie Slide) ride in the world. Imagine the Adrenalin rush traveling a speed of 106 km’s hurtling 425 m across the gorge, while suspended 120 m above the breath taking beauty of the Zambezi water below!

As the river zigzags down the Batoka Gorges, our cable is suspended across from one side to the other. For this product you are harnessed and attached to a pulley, then launched over the edge picking up speed as you descend over the water and reaching a speed of 106 km an hour.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('316','8','en','Sundowner Cruise','sundowner-cruise-9','The Zambezi Sunset cruise is a superb way to relax and enjoy the Spectacular beauty of the Zambezi River.

There are great photo opportunities against often-spectacular African sunsets.

Flocks of birds skim the waterline as the sun sets behind the African skyline. Clients may have the opportunity to see a variety of game; including hippo, crocodile, and elephant as well as enjoy the many different bird species.

The Sunset cruise is very popular and includes finger snacks, beer, wine, local spirits and soft drinks.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('317','9','en','Elephant Encounter','elephant-encounter-11','The Elephant Encounter affords guests the opportunity to unobtrusively interact with some of the biggest personalities in Africa, in a pristine wilderness environment overflowing with raw natural beauty. Guests spend time and connect with elephants in the most positive and natural way possible.

An open-design thatch Boma gives guests an uninterrupted view of the beautiful Masuwe River, and against this breath-taking back drop, guests will be given an insightful and educational presentation on the Pearls Tourss Elephant Sanctuary and Orphange. The sanctuary was founded on the principle of conservation, and one of the most effective ways to evoke a sense of environmental responsibility is to show what stands to be lost.
Guests will have an opportunity to talk to guides that have journeyed – physically and metaphorically, incredible distances with these elephant , and learn more about the complexities of the individuals and the herd structures. Guests will learn about the elephant as well as their history and how they came to be in our care as well as the threats facing elephant populations today, in an interesting and informative talk.
Guests will venture out into the bush to spend time with the elephant and the sight of the gentle grey mammals up close and personal will be imprinted on guests’ minds’ long after they have returned home. Witness the special relationship the elephant keepers share with the animals and become a part of it. You will have the opportunity to take photographs with the elephants, marvel at their size and watch them behaving normally; browsing and interacting with one another.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('318','10','en','Elephant interaction & Lunch','elephant-interaction--lunch-12','Elephants',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('319','11','en','Elephant Art','elephant-art-13','The Pearls Tourss Elephant Sanctuary and Art of Africa have teamed up to create an eco conscious and unique elephant experience, brought to life by the artistic strokes of your fingertips, while surrounded by the African bush.

An open-design thatch Boma gives guests an uninterrupted view of the beautiful Masuwe River, and against this breath-taking back drop, guests will be given an insightful and educational presentation on the Pearls Tourss Elephant Sanctuary and Orphange.
The sanctuary was founded on the principle of conservation, and one of the most effective ways to evoke a sense of environmental responsibility is to show what stands to be lost. Guests will have an opportunity to talk to guides that have journeyed – physically and metaphorically, incredible distances with these elephant, and learn more about the complexities of the individuals and the herd structures. Guests will learn about the elephant as well as their history and how they came to be in our care as well as the threats facing elephant populations today, in an interesting and informative talk.

Guests then venture down to a waterhole and mud wallow where, under the shade of an enormous Mopane tree, they will find a chair and easel – each set up with a fresh sheet of paper. Brightly coloured aprons and palettes with bright splotches of paint will also be handed out.
A private tutor is provided to guide guests through a painting workshop, using their sketch pads and brush to capture the moment. Soon guests’ white sheets of paper will be transformed into a canvas with a glorious blue sky, sunshine, yellow, brown or green grass and of course elephants.
Once finished, guests will go back to “The Wallow” for a delicious two course buffet lunch accompanied by a cold beverage rounding off a perfect morning’s experience. After lunch guests will be transferred back to their lodgings in Victoria Falls Town.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('320','12','en','Gorge Swing — Batoka Gorge','gorge-swing-14','<p>Stand 70m above the raging Zambezi and take the ultimate leap of faith. The Gorge Swing launches you into free fall before swinging you in a massive 90-metre arc above the Batoka Gorge. Victoria Falls\'s signature adrenaline experience.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `bc_tour_translations` (id,origin_id,locale,title,slug,content,short_desc,address,faqs,create_user,update_user,created_at,updated_at,include,exclude,itinerary,surrounding) VALUES ('321','13','en','Microlight Flight over Victoria Falls','microlight-flight-victoria-falls','<p>For the ultimate open-air flying experience, take to the skies in a microlight and soar directly over Victoria Falls from the Zambia side. Feel the spray and hear the thunder in an open cockpit. Choose 12/15 minutes or extend to 25/30 minutes.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7',NULL,'2026-05-26 00:23:26','2026-05-26 00:23:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
