s ($150-200) • Alcohol • Pre-trek accommodation • Post-trek accommodation</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 7 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1395.00',NULL,'70','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"Why choose Lemosho over other routes?\",\"content\":\"Remote, scenic, fewer crowds. Excellent acclimatization over 7 days. High success rate (85%+). Beautiful Shira Plateau crossing rarely crowded.\"},{\"title\":\"Is Lemosho harder than Machame?\",\"content\":\"Not harder, better. Same final ascent as Machame but 7 days instead of 6. Extra acclimatization day on Shira Plateau significantly helps.\"},{\"title\":\"How many people on this route?\",\"content\":\"Much fewer than Machame or Marangu. Remote approach keeps numbers low. More intimate experience with nature and guides. Quiet experience preferred.\"},{\"title\":\"What\'s the scenery like?\",\"content\":\"Rainforest entry, moorland, Shira Plateau (most scenic), volcanic alpine zone. Diverse and stunning. Fewer people to share it with.\"},{\"title\":\"Is this suitable for first-timers?\",\"content\":\"Yes! The 7-day format and good acclimatization make this ideal for first-time trekkers. High success rate reflects this.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Licensed mountain guides\",\"Professional porters (ethical)\",\"Sleeping bag and mattress\",\"All meals (fresh daily)\",\"Mountain hut accommodations\",\"Park entrance fees\",\"Emergency oxygen provided\",\"Summit certificate\",\"Cooking and dining equipment\",\"Hot water for washing\",\"First aid and health monitoring\",\"Rescue insurance\"]','[\"International flights\",\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\",\"Personal climbing gear (rent available)\",\"Tips ($150-200 suggested)\",\"Alcohol\",\"Pre-trek accommodation\",\"Post-trek accommodation\",\"Personal medications\"]','[{\"title\":\"Day 1: Londorossi to Mti Mkubwa\",\"desc\":\"Forest trek to Big Tree camp\",\"content\":\"Drive to Londorossi Gate (2,100m), 4WD to Lemosho Glades (2,400m). Trek through dense forest to Mti Mkubwa (Big Tree) Camp (2,800m). Afternoon rest and acclimatization begins.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 2: Mti Mkubwa to Shira 2\",\"desc\":\"Enter Shira Plateau\",\"content\":\"Trek through heather moorland, ascending Shira Ridge. Enter beautiful Shira Plateau (3,500m). Spectacular views of both Kibo and Mawenzi peaks. Camp at Shira 2 (3,850m).\"},{\"title\":\"Day 3: Shira Plateau Acclimatization\",\"desc\":\"Gentle plateau walk\",\"content\":\"Gentle acclimatization walk across Shira Plateau. No pressure, enjoy the scenery. Outstanding views of volcanic peaks. Rest well for altitude ahead. Sleep at Shira 2.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 4: Shira to Barranco\",\"desc\":\"Lava Tower acclimatization\",\"content\":\"Hike via Lava Tower (4,600m) for altitude exposure. Descend to Barranco Camp (3,900m). \\\\\\\"Climb high, sleep low\\\\\\\" strategy proves effective. Evening rest.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 5: Barranco Wall Climb\",\"desc\":\"Non-technical climbing\",\"content\":\"Climb Barranco Wall (4-5 hours). Steep but non-technical scrambling. Reach Karanga Camp (4,000m). Stunning views reward your effort.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 6: Barafu Base Camp\",\"desc\":\"Final camp before summit\",\"content\":\"Continue ascending to Barafu Camp (4,640m). Complete South Circuit. Rest, hydrate, early dinner. Mental preparation for summit night.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 7: Summit & Descent\",\"desc\":\"Uhuru Peak to Mweka\",\"content\":\"Midnight summit attempt via Stella Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Sunrise celebration. Long descent to Mweka Camp. Certificate and celebration dinner.\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
