 • Personal gear • Tips ($150-200) • Alcohol • Pre-trek accommodation • Post-trek accommodation</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 8 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1495.00',NULL,'80','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"How much does the extra day help?\",\"content\":\"Significantly! Two days on Shira Plateau (our highest natural acclimatization area) substantially improves success rates. 90%+ success rate reflects this.\"},{\"title\":\"Is this the easiest high-altitude trek?\",\"content\":\"Yes. Maximum time, maximum acclimatization. Low daily mileage. Highest success rate of any Kilimanjaro route. Ideal for inexperienced high-altitude trekkers.\"},{\"title\":\"What do I do on the extra plateau day?\",\"content\":\"Gentle walks, scenic photo stops, complete rest, extensive hydration. No pressure to reach any distance. Guides adjust based on how you\'re feeling.\"},{\"title\":\"Is this suitable for anyone?\",\"content\":\"Anyone with moderate fitness can succeed! Age is not the limiting factor\\u2014acclimatization and determination are. We\'ve had 75-year-olds summit successfully.\"},{\"title\":\"Why isn\'t everyone doing 8 days?\",\"content\":\"Cost and time. 8 days is more expensive and takes longer. But for serious trekkers and first-timers, it\'s worth every penny.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Licensed mountain guides\",\"Professional porters (ethical wages)\",\"Sleeping bag and mattress\",\"All meals (fresh prepared)\",\"Mountain hut accommodations\",\"Park entrance fees\",\"Emergency oxygen available\",\"Summit certificate\",\"Cooking and dining equipment\",\"Hot water for washing\",\"First aid and monitoring\",\"Rescue insurance included\",\"Extra acclimatization day on Shira\"]','[\"International flights\",\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\",\"Personal climbing gear (rent available)\",\"Tips ($150-200 suggested)\",\"Alcohol\",\"Pre-trek accommodation\",\"Post-trek accommodation\",\"Personal medications\"]','[{\"title\":\"Day 1: Londorossi to Mti Mkubwa\",\"desc\":\"Forest entry\",\"content\":\"Drive to Londorossi, 4WD to Lemosho Glades. Forest trek to Mti Mkubwa (Big Tree) Camp (2,800m). Afternoon rest and introduction to trekking adventure.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 2: Mti Mkubwa to Shira 1\",\"desc\":\"Moorland ascent\",\"content\":\"Trek through heather moorland. Ascend Shira Ridge. Arrive at Shira 1 Camp (3,500m). First views of Kibo and Mawenzi. Exciting mountain scenery.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 3: Shira 1 to Shira 2\",\"desc\":\"Gentle plateau walk\",\"content\":\"Gentle hike across beautiful Shira Plateau. Prime acclimatization. No pressure. Exceptional views of volcanic peaks. Sleep at Shira 2 (3,850m). Feel your body adapting.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 4: Shira Plateau Extended\",\"desc\":\"Extra acclimatization day\",\"content\":\"Another day on Shira Plateau! Gentle walk to scenic viewpoint. Rest, hydrate, enjoy the plateau. Critical extra acclimatization. Sleep at Shira 2.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 5: Shira to Barranco\",\"desc\":\"Lava Tower acclimatization hike\",\"content\":\"Hike via Lava Tower (4,600m) for acclimatization benefit. Descend to Barranco Camp (3,900m). \\\\\\\"Climb high, sleep low\\\\\\\" proven strategy. Evening rest.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 6: Barranco Wall Climb\",\"desc\":\"Non-technical steep climb\",\"content\":\"Climb Barranco Wall (4-5 hours). Exciting scrambling. Reach Karanga Camp (4,000m). Prepare mentally for final climb.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 7: Barafu Base Camp\",\"desc\":\"Summit camp\",\"content\":\"Final ascent to Barafu Camp (4,640m). Complete South Circuit. Rest thoroughly. Hydrate well. Early dinner. Mental and physical prep for summit night.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 8: Summit & Descent\",\"desc\":\"Uhuru Peak sunrise & celebration\",\"content\":\"Midnight departure. Climb via Stella Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Sunrise at top of Africa. Descend to Mweka Camp. Celebration with entire team. Certificates and congratulations.\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
