accommodation • Post-trek accommodation</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 6 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1295.00',NULL,'60','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"Why choose the hardest route?\",\"content\":\"For experienced trekkers seeking a challenge. Steep and demanding but incredibly rewarding. Fewer people on this route means more solitude.\"},{\"title\":\"What is the success rate?\",\"content\":\"60% due to difficulty. Most failures occur on Day 1-2 when the steep gradient is most challenging. Requires good fitness and determination.\"},{\"title\":\"Is Umbwe recommended for first-timers?\",\"content\":\"No. Not suitable for inexperienced high-altitude trekkers. Better to start with Marangu or Lemosho. Umbwe for experienced mountaineers.\"},{\"title\":\"How steep are Days 1-2?\",\"content\":\"Very steep! 50%+ gradient on some sections. Your quads will burn. Most demanding part is the first two days. If you survive that, you\'ve got this.\"},{\"title\":\"What\'s the advantage of this route?\",\"content\":\"Fewest people (solo or small groups), fastest ascent (6 days), dramatic rainforest-to-alpine transition, incredibly scenic. For skilled trekkers.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Licensed mountain guides\",\"Professional porters\",\"Sleeping bag and mattress\",\"All meals prepared fresh\",\"Mountain camp accommodations\",\"Park entrance fees\",\"Emergency oxygen\",\"Summit certificates\",\"Cooking and dining equipment\",\"Hot water provided\",\"First aid and monitoring\",\"Rescue insurance\"]','[\"International flights\",\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\",\"Personal climbing gear (rent available)\",\"Tips ($150-200 suggested)\",\"Alcohol\",\"Pre-trek accommodation\",\"Post-trek accommodation\",\"Personal medications\"]','[{\"title\":\"Day 1: Umbwe Gate to Camp\",\"desc\":\"Steep rainforest climb\",\"content\":\"Drive to Umbwe Gate (1,640m). Begin steep trek through dense rainforest. See exotic birds, monkeys, lush ferns. Challenging start. Camp at Umbwe Cave (2,700m). Rest well.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 2: Umbwe to Barranco\",\"desc\":\"Forest to alpine transition\",\"content\":\"Continue steep ascent out of rainforest. Enter moorland. Views of Kilimanjaro open up. Descend to Barranco Camp (3,900m). Challenging day tests your fitness.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 3: Barranco Wall Climb\",\"desc\":\"Famous rock scramble\",\"content\":\"Climb Barranco Wall (4-5 hours). Steep, non-technical scrambling with chains. Reach Karanga Camp (4,000m). Feeling altitude now. Rest and hydrate thoroughly.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 4: Barafu Base Camp\",\"desc\":\"Final ascent\",\"content\":\"Continue climbing to Barafu Camp (4,640m). Complete South Circuit. Rest, eat well, sleep. Prepare mentally for midnight summit attempt.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 5: Summit Attempt\",\"desc\":\"Midnight climb to Uhuru Peak\",\"content\":\"Midnight departure. Climb via Stella Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Sunrise celebration. Descend to Mweka Camp (3,100m). Long day but incredible achievement.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 6: Descent & Departure\",\"desc\":\"Rainforest descent & recovery\",\"content\":\"Final descent through rainforest to Mweka Gate (1,640m). Receive summit certificates. Transfer to Moshi for well-earned rest and celebration.\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
