ek accommodation • Post-trek accommodation</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 7 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1395.00',NULL,'70','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"Why the northern approach?\",\"content\":\"Unique views of Kenya landscape. Fewer crowds (less popular than Marangu\\/Machame). Excellent acclimatization profile. High success rate (85%+).\"},{\"title\":\"How is the northern route less crowded?\",\"content\":\"Most trekkers use Machame or Marangu. Rongai is \\\\\\\"the secret route.\\\\\\\" Northern approach, fewer outfitters. Quiet experience preferred by many.\"},{\"title\":\"What are the Kenyan plains views like?\",\"content\":\"From Rongai Gate and early camps, you see into Kenya. Unique perspective. Most routes face southward. This directional variation is special.\"},{\"title\":\"How does success rate compare?\",\"content\":\"85%+ for 7-day Rongai, excellent acclimatization. Slower pace than Umbwe. Scenic route with manageable challenge. Underrated for success-seekers.\"},{\"title\":\"Is this good for first-timers?\",\"content\":\"Yes! Rongai offers excellent acclimatization, high success rate, and fewer crowds. Less crowded than Machame but slightly more challenging than Marangu. Good balance.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Licensed mountain guides\",\"Professional porters\",\"Sleeping bag and mattress\",\"All meals prepared fresh\",\"Mountain hut accommodations\",\"Park entrance fees\",\"Emergency oxygen\",\"Summit certificates\",\"Cooking and dining equipment\",\"Hot water provided\",\"First aid and monitoring\",\"Rescue insurance\"]','[\"International flights\",\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\",\"Personal climbing gear (rent available)\",\"Tips ($150-200 suggested)\",\"Alcohol\",\"Pre-trek accommodation\",\"Post-trek accommodation\",\"Personal medications\"]','[{\"title\":\"Day 1: Rongai Gate to Simba Camp\",\"desc\":\"Northern entry through farm fields\",\"content\":\"Drive to Rongai Gate (1,950m), unique northern approach. Trek through farmland and pine forest. See Kenya landscape to the north. Arrive at Simba Camp (2,600m). Evening rest.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 2: Simba to Second Cave\",\"desc\":\"Steady ascent with views\",\"content\":\"Steady ascent to Second Cave (3,450m). Views of Kibo and eastern ice fields develop. Moorland opens up. Camp with outstanding vistas. Rest and acclimatize.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 3: Second to Kikelewa Cave\",\"desc\":\"Continue toward Kibo\",\"content\":\"Trek toward Kibo. Reach Kikelewa Cave (3,600m). Big-mountain views open fully. Alpine desert landscape. Cold exposed camp. Prepare for altitude ahead.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 4: Kikelewa to Mawenzi Tarn\",\"desc\":\"Approach the saddle\",\"content\":\"Short steep climb to Mawenzi Tarn (4,330m) beneath Mawenzi peaks. Spectacular crater views. Important acclimatization day. Rest well. Hydrate thoroughly.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 5: Mawenzi to Kibo Hut\",\"desc\":\"Cross the saddle\",\"content\":\"Cross lunar desert Saddle between Kibo and Mawenzi. Arrive at Kibo Hut (4,703m). Final rest before summit. Early dinner and sleep prep.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 6: Summit Attempt\",\"desc\":\"Uhuru Peak via Gilman\'s Point\",\"content\":\"Pre-dawn start (11pm). Climb via Gilman\'s Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Sunrise celebration. Descend to Horombo Hut (3,720m). Marangu-side descent begins.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 7: Descent to Marangu Gate\",\"desc\":\"Final forest descent\",\"content\":\"Descend through moorland and forest to Marangu Gate (1,844m). Receive certificates. Transfer to Moshi. Celebrate your achievement!\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
INSERT INTO `bc_tours` (id,title,slug,content,image_id,banner_image_id,short_desc,category_id,location_id,address,map_lat,map_lng,map_zoom,is_featured,gallery,video,price,sale_price,duration,time_slot,zone,activity_type,available_months,available_days,tsokanew_id,min_people,max_people,faqs,status,publish_date,create_user,update_user,deleted_at,origin_id,lang,created_at,updated_at,default_state,enable_fixed_date,start_date,end_date,last_booking_date,include,exclude,itinerary,review_score,ical_import_url,enable_service_fee,service_fee,surrounding,author_id,booking_type,limit_type,capacity_type,capacity,pass_exprire_type,pass_exprire_at,pass_valid_for,date_select_type,min_day_before_booking,is_package) VALUES ('422','6-Day Rongai Trek','6-day-rongai-trek','<div style=\'font-family:Arial,sans-serif;\'><h1 style=\'color:#FF6B35; font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;\'>Northern Approach - Good Acclimatization</h1><p style=\'font-size:15px; color:#555; margin:15px 0; line-height:1.8;\'>Compact Rongai Route with northern approach through pristine landscapes. Good acclimatization over 6 days with beautiful views and lower crowds.</p><div style=\'background:#f9f5ec; padding:12px; border-radius:6px; margin:20px 0; border-left:4px solid #FF6B35;\'><strong>Highlights:</strong><br><span>Northern Approach • Lower Crowds • Good Acclimatization • Kenyan Plains Views • Moderate Difficulty • 6-Day Compact • Scenic Beauty</span></div><h3 style=\'color:#2ECC71; margin:25px 0 10px 0; border-bottom:2px solid #2ECC71; padding-bottom:8px;\'>✓ What\'s Included</h3><p>Licensed guides • Professional porters • Sleeping bag and mattress • All meals • Mountain huts • Park fees • Emergency oxygen • Summit certificate • Cooking equipment • Hot water</p><h3 style=\'color:#E74C3C; margin:25px 0 10px 0; border-bottom:2px solid #E74C3C; padding-bottom:8px;\'>✗ What\'s NOT Included</h3><p>International flights • Travel insurance REQUIRED • Personal gear • Tips ($150-200) • Alcohol • Pre-trek accommodation • Post-trek accommodation</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 6 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1195.00',NULL,'60','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"Is 6 days sufficient for Rongai?\",\"content\":\"Good acclimatization for 6 days. 80% success rate. Not as many acclimatization opportunities as 7-day, but still excellent compared to 5-day alternatives.\"},{\"title\":\"Why choose 6-day over 7-day?\",\"content\":\"Cost and time savings. Still get Rongai\'s unique northern experience and low-crowd advantage. 80% vs 85% success\\u2014acceptable trade-off for many trekkers.\"},{\"title\":\"What about the cold camps?\",\"content\":\"Kikelewa Cave (3,600m) and Mawenzi Tarn (4,330m) are cold and exposed. Bringer sleeping bag rated to -10\\u00b0C. Nights are challenging but manageable.\"},{\"title\":\"How difficult is Day 3 (Kikelewa to Mawenzi)?\",\"content\":\"Steep 900m elevation gain. But it\'s a short day (2-3 hours). Important rest for acclimatization. Many find it challenging but short enough to manage.\"},{\"title\":\"Can I step up from 6 to 7 days?\",\"content\":\"Yes! If you\'re acclimatizing well and want more buffer, guides can adjust. Conversely, if struggling, pace slows. Flexibility available based on health.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"Licensed mountain guides\",\"Professional porters\",\"Sleeping bag and mattress\",\"All meals (fresh prepared)\",\"Mountain hut\\/camp accommodations\",\"Park entrance fees\",\"Emergency oxygen available\",\"Summit certificates\",\"Cooking and dining equipment\",\"Hot water for washing\",\"First aid and monitoring\",\"Rescue insurance\"]','[\"International flights\",\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\",\"Personal climbing gear (rent available)\",\"Tips ($150-200 suggested)\",\"Alcohol\",\"Pre-trek accommodation\",\"Post-trek accommodation\",\"Personal medications\"]','[{\"title\":\"Day 1: Rongai Gate to 1st Caves Camp\",\"desc\":\"Northern entry through farmland\",\"content\":\"Drive to Rongai Gate (1,950m), northern approach. Trek through cornfields and pine forest. Kenyan plains views. Arrive at 1st Caves Camp (2,650m). Rest after first day.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 2: 1st to Kikelewa Cave\",\"desc\":\"Ascend past Second Cave\",\"content\":\"Cold breakfast then ascend. Pass Second Cave, continue toward Kibo. Reach Kikelewa Cave (3,600m). Big-mountain views. Cold exposed camp. Prepare for altitude.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 3: Kikelewa to Mawenzi Tarn\",\"desc\":\"Short steep climb & acclimatization\",\"content\":\"Short steep trail to Mawenzi Tarn Camp (4,330m). Beneath Mawenzi crater spires. Spectacular views. Important rest day. Feel your body adapting to altitude.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 4: Mawenzi Tarn to Kibo Hut\",\"desc\":\"Cross the Saddle\",\"content\":\"Half-day hike east across lunar Saddle to Kibo Hut (4,703m). Early dinner before night summit. Rest and prepare mentally and physically.\"},{\"title\":\"Day 5: Summit Attempt\",\"desc\":\"Uhuru Peak via Gilman\'s Point\",\"content\":\"Midnight departure. Climb via Gilman\'s Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Sunrise at Africa\'s highest point. Descend to Horombo Hut (3,720m).\"},{\"title\":\"Day 6: Descent & Celebration\",\"desc\":\"Marangu Gate descent & certificates\",\"content\":\"After celebration breakfast, descend to Marangu Gate (1,844m). Receive summit certificates. Transfer to Moshi. Well-deserved celebration with your team!\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
INSERT INTO `bc_tours` (id,title,slug,content,image_id,banner_image_id,short_desc,category_id,location_id,address,map_lat,map_lng,map_zoom,is_featured,gallery,video,price,sale_price,duration,time_slot,zone,activity_type,available_months,available_days,tsokanew_id,min_people,max_people,faqs,status,publish_date,create_user,update_user,deleted_at,origin_id,lang,created_at,updated_at,default_state,enable_fixed_date,start_date,end_date,last_booking_date,include,exclude,itinerary,review_score,ical_import_url,enable_service_fee,service_fee,surrounding,author_id,booking_type,limit_type,capacity_type,capacity,pass_exprire_type,pass_exprire_at,pass_valid_for,date_select_type,min_day_before_booking,is_package) VALUES ('423','8-Day Northern Circuit Trek','8-day-northern-circuit-trek','<div style=\'font-family:Arial,sans-serif;\'><h1 style=\'color:#FF6B35; font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;\'>Kilimanjaro\'s Ultimate Route - 90%+ Success Rate</h1><p style=\'font-size:15px; color:#555; margin:15px 0; line-height:1.8;\'>Trek around Kilimanjaro\'s northern slopes with dramatic views of both Kibo and Mawenzi. The longest route offers the best acclimatization and highest summit success.</p><div style=\'background:#f9f5ec; padding:12px; border-radius:6px; margin:20px 0; border-left:4px solid #FF6B35;\'><strong>Highlights:</strong><br><span>Londorossi Route • Shira Plateau • Lava Tower Acclimatization • Barranco Wall Climb • Both Peaks Visible • Highest Success Rate • Full Circumnavigation</span></div><h3 style=\'color:#2ECC71; margin:25px 0 10px 0; border-bottom:2px solid #2ECC71; padding-bottom:8px;\'>✓ What\'s Included</h3><p>Licensed guides • Professional porters • Sleeping bag and mattress • All meals • Mountain accommodations • Park fees • Emergency oxygen • Summit certificate • Cooking equipment • Hot water</p><h3 style=\'color:#E74C3C; margin:25px 0 10px 0; border-bottom:2px solid #E74C3C; padding-bottom:8px;\'>✗ What\'s NOT Included</h3><p>International flights • Travel insurance REQUIRED • Personal gear • Tips ($150-200) • Alcohol • Pre-trek accommodation • Post-trek accommodation • Personal meds</p></div>',NULL,NULL,'Multi-day Trek package - 8 days from Mount Kilimanjaro','1','13','Mount Kilimanjaro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1695.00',NULL,'80','1','2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"What is the success rate?\",\"content\":\"90%+ for 8-day routes with proper acclimatization. Success depends on individual fitness, determination, and proper pacing by guides.\"},{\"title\":\"Do I need prior climbing experience?\",\"content\":\"No experience needed. Good cardiovascular fitness and mental determination are more important than technical skills.\"},{\"title\":\"What about altitude sickness?\",\"content\":\"We use gradual ascent and proper rest days to minimize risk. Guides monitor health continuously. \\\"Climb high, sleep low\\\" strategy helps.\"},{\"title\":\"How hard is the Barranco Wall?\",\"content\":\"Steep but not technical. No ropes or special equipment needed. Scrambling with chains available. 4-5 hours. Difficult but achievable for fit people.\"},{\"title\":\"What if I cannot summit?\",\"content\":\"Safety is paramount. Many trekkers reach 4,600m (higher than Mont Blanc). Summit isn\'t mandatory\\u2014the experience matters most.\"},{\"title\":\"Is the food good on the mountain?\",\"content\":\"Yes! Porters and cook prepare fresh meals: soups, rice, vegetables, meat. High-altitude cooking is challenging but quality is maintained.\"},{\"title\":\"How are porters treated?\",\"content\":\"Fair wages, limits on load weight (15kg max), rest days, proper meals, health insurance. We use ethical porter practices.\"},{\"title\":\"What fitness training is needed?\",\"content\":\"Train 3 months: stair climbing, hill hiking, running. Build cardiovascular fitness. On the mountain you\'ll run 20+ km total.\"}]','publish',NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-31 17:08:05','2026-05-31 17:08:05','1','0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"title\":\"Licensed mountain guides (IFMGA trained)\"},{\"title\":\"Professional porters (one per trekker)\"},{\"title\":\"Sleeping bag and foam mattress\"},{\"title\":\"All meals prepared fresh daily\"},{\"title\":\"Mountain hut accommodations\"},{\"title\":\"Park entrance fees\"},{\"title\":\"Emergency oxygen and medical kit\"},{\"title\":\"Summit certificates\"},{\"title\":\"Cooking and dining equipment\"},{\"title\":\"Hot water for washing\"},{\"title\":\"Rescue insurance\"},{\"title\":\"First aid and health monitoring\"}]','[{\"title\":\"International flights\"},{\"title\":\"Travel insurance (REQUIRED)\"},{\"title\":\"Personal climbing gear (available to rent)\"},{\"title\":\"Tips for guides\\/porters ($150-200 suggested)\"},{\"title\":\"Alcoholic beverages\"},{\"title\":\"Pre-trek acclimatization (optional 1-2 nights)\"},{\"title\":\"Post-trek accommodation\"},{\"title\":\"Personal medications\"},{\"title\":\"Airport transfers\"},{\"title\":\"Personal travel insurance\"}]','[{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 1: Londorossi Gate to Mti Mkubwa\",\"desc\":\"Forest trek to Big Tree camp\",\"content\":\"Drive to Londorossi Gate (2,100m), register, and begin trek through rainforest. Hike to Mti Mkubwa (Big Tree) camp at 2,800m. Afternoon rest and acclimatization.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 2: Mti Mkubwa to Shira 2 Camp\",\"desc\":\"Cross Shira Ridge onto plateau\",\"content\":\"Ascend through heather moorland, crossing Shira Ridge. Arrive at Shira 2 Camp (3,500m). Diverse vegetation and spectacular views of both Kibo and Mawenzi peaks.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 3: Shira Plateau Acclimatization\",\"desc\":\"Gentle plateau walk & rest\",\"content\":\"Acclimatization day with gentle hike across Shira Plateau. Outstanding views of Kibo and Mawenzi. Rest well to prepare body for altitude ahead.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 4: Shira to Barranco Camp\",\"desc\":\"Lava Tower acclimatization hike\",\"content\":\"Hike via Lava Tower (4,600m) for acclimatization benefit, then descend to Barranco Camp (3,900m). Important strategy: \\\"climb high, sleep low\\\" for better adaptation.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 5: Barranco to Karanga Camp\",\"desc\":\"Climb Barranco Wall\",\"content\":\"Climb the famous Barranco Wall (steep but not technical), traverse to Karanga Valley. Camp at 4,000m. Start feeling altitude impact.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 6: Karanga to Barafu Camp\",\"desc\":\"Final ascent to base camp\",\"content\":\"Continue climbing to Barafu Camp (4,640m), completing the South Circuit route. This is your final camp before summit attempt. Rest and prepare.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 7: Summit Attempt\",\"desc\":\"Midnight climb to Uhuru Peak\",\"content\":\"Midnight departure (around 11pm). Climb via Stella Point to Uhuru Peak (5,895m). Arrive at sunrise. Celebrate at Africa\'s highest point. Descend to Mweka Hut.\"},{\"image_id\":null,\"title\":\"Day 8: Final Descent to Mweka Gate\",\"desc\":\"Rainforest descent & certificates\",\"content\":\"Final descent through rainforest to Mweka Gate (1,640m). Receive summit certificates. Transfer to Moshi for rest and celebration.\"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0');
